cards.body:
In December 2021 the FCA fined **HSBC Bank plc** about **GBP 63.9m** for failings in its anti-money laundering processes. HSBC monitored hundreds of millions of transactions a month with automated systems, but three key parts had serious weaknesses from 2010 to 2018. HSBC failed to:
- check whether its monitoring **scenarios covered the relevant risks**, and to risk-assess new scenarios in good time;
- properly **test and update the parameters** that decided whether a transaction looked suspicious;
- check the **accuracy and completeness of the data** feeding the systems.

HSBC settled early and received a 30% discount from about GBP 91.4m.

**Lesson:** a monitoring system is only as good as its scenarios, thresholds and data. Someone senior must own and test all three. Source: FCA press release, 17 December 2021.
